From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Turn the component updater off in a Windows browser

Append --disable-component-update to the Windows browser process's
command line after the application's OnBeforeCommandLineProcessing, so
a client cannot drop it. In the Rockstar launcher's Open the updater
started about a minute after the page: its BITS downloads asked COM
for BackgroundCopyManager (rpcss and a dllhost each time) and its
unpacking started Unzipper utilities, each one more process and JIT
pool copy under Playport (PLA-394). Social Club does not update
Chromium components. Apply to the CEF pin before its stock Chromium
patcher runs.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-cef-late-children.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 libcef/common/chrome/chrome_main_delegate_cef.cc |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libcef/common/chrome/chrome_main_delegate_cef.cc b/libcef/common/chrome/chrome_main_delegate_cef.cc
index cd5203bee..69ce418f2 100644
--- a/libcef/common/chrome/chrome_main_delegate_cef.cc
+++ b/libcef/common/chrome/chrome_main_delegate_cef.cc
@@ -387,6 +387,15 @@ std::optional<int> ChromeMainDelegateCef::BasicStartupComplete() {
     std::ignore = commandLinePtr->Detach(nullptr);
   }
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  // No component updater in the browser: its BITS downloads start COM
+  // servers (rpcss, dllhost) and its unpacking starts Unzipper utilities.
+  // Added after the application's hook so that it stays on.
+  if (process_type.empty()) {
+    command_line->AppendSwitch(switches::kDisableComponentUpdate);
+  }
+#endif
+
   // Call as early as possible.
   InitLogging(command_line);
 
